## Why This Is Asked
Governance, permissions, and drift detection are critical in multi-account SAP deployments. This question tests practical use of IAM roles, SCPs, AWS Config, and automated reporting within AWS-native tooling.

## Key Concepts
- IAM roles bound to SAP modules
- Service Control Policies for least privilege
- AWS Config custom rules for drift detection
- Daily Lambda reports to S3 with SNS notifications
- CDK for module-role bindings and SCPs

## Code Example
```typescript
// CDK snippet: module → role → restrictive SCP
const moduleRole = new iam.Role(this, 'SAPModuleRole', {
  assumedBy: new iam.ServicePrincipal('ec2.amazonaws.com'),
  description: 'SAP module specific role'
});
moduleRole.addToPolicy(new iam.PolicyStatement({
  actions: ['ec2:DescribeInstances'],
  resources: ['*']
}));
new iam.Policy(this, 'SAPModuleBoundPolicy', {
  roles: [moduleRole],
  // restrictive permissions posted here
});
// Config rule and SCP creation would follow similarly
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test and simulate drift to verify alerts?
- How would you scale this approach across many SAP modules and accounts?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of AWS patching automation, SAP patching options, health checks, rollback strategies, and CloudFormation for operational guardrails.

## Key Concepts
- AWS Systems Manager Maintenance Windows
- SAP patching options: SUM vs OS patches
- Pre/post patch validation: SAPControl, SAP background jobs, host metrics
- Rollback strategies: SAP backups, AMI snapshots
- CloudFormation for roles and patch baselines

## Code Example
```javascript
// CFN skeleton (pseudo)
{
  "AWSTemplateFormatVersion": "2010-09-09",
  "Resources": {
    "SAPSSMRole": {
      "Type": "AWS::IAM::Role",
      "Properties": {
        "AssumeRolePolicyDocument": { "Version": "2012-10-17", "Statement": [ { "Effect": "Allow", "Principal": { "Service": ["ec2.amazonaws.com", "ssm.amazonaws.com"] }, "Action": "sts:AssumeRole" } ] },
        "ManagedPolicyArns": [ "arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonSSMFullAccess" ]
      }
    },
    "SAPPatchBaseline": {
      "Type": "AWS::SSM::PatchBaseline",
      "Properties": {
        "Name": "SAPBaseline",
        "OperatingSystem": "AmazonLinux2"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you verify patch success in SAP and the OS without impacting production?
- How would you extend to multi-region DR alignment and scoped approvals?
